**Cucumber-like odor of hydrozoan jelly fish *Spirocodon saltatrix***

Michiya KAMIO\*, Hiroshi NAGAI\*

Department of Ocean Sciences, Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology, Minato, Tokyo 108-8477

**Abstract** Medusae of *Spirocodon saltatrix* smell like cucumber because they release (*E*)-2-nonenal and
(*E*,*Z*)-2,6-nonadienal. These compounds are theoretically derived from polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFA)
and might have biological functions as defensive molecule and/or chemical signal.
